# The pedal root's packages, beyond mmdebstrap's minbase: read by the image build (step 4 of
# docs/vip-image.md), from the pinned snapshot, without recommends. What each is for:

# The kernel: the STOCK Ubuntu RT flavour — the fallback the spare slot boots (rtpi
# devices/vip/device.env, FALLBACK_KERNEL) — and the Pi 5's WiFi firmware. The pedal's own kernel,
# rtpi's rebuild, is in no archive: the image build installs it from hash-pinned artefacts
# (devices/vip/image.lock, docs/vip-kernel-image.md).
linux-image-7.0.0-1017-raspi-realtime
linux-modules-7.0.0-1017-raspi-realtime
linux-firmware-raspi
wireless-regdb

# Booting and the boot selection (rtpi's vip-boot: python3, dracut, the FAT tools).
systemd
systemd-sysv
systemd-resolved
systemd-timesyncd
udev
dbus
dracut-core
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
# Used by vip-boot, pedald and pedal-diag
python3
# pedal-data grows to fill the card on first boot.
systemd-repart

# Reaching it.
openssh-server
sudo
wpasupplicant
iproute2
iputils-ping
ca-certificates
# scripts/sync-library copies the model and IR library with it.
rsync

# The codec (pedal-codec) and the engine's tools (alsa-utils: amixer, alsactl, arecord).
raspi-utils-dt
device-tree-compiler
alsa-utils

# Reading the board itself: `vcgencmd` (firmware config, throttling, the bootloader's own report)
# and `rpi-eeprom-config`/`rpi-eeprom-update`. Added 2026-10-05 to answer whether the bootloader
# had changed under a UART fault that was not the firmware's fault after all (pedal.project
# bench-results/2026-10-05-header-uart-disabled.md). Note that rpi-eeprom ships a unit which
# *applies* a pending bootloader update at every boot; it is listed in etc/pedal/masked-units,
# because flashing the EEPROM is a decision rather than a side effect of an image.
raspi-utils
rpi-eeprom

# pedal-tune, pedal-device, pedald (chown and stty are coreutils).
procps
util-linux
kmod
less

# pedal-diag
i2c-tools
